# Create pull request (docker-awx-mcp)

Run all git/gh commands from the **docker-awx-mcp/** repo root (`mystack-cloud/docker-awx-mcp`).

## Before opening

Run in parallel:

```bash
git status
git diff && git diff --staged
git log -5 --oneline
git branch -vv
```

Review all commits that will land on the PR (not only the latest).

## Branch and push

Branch names use the same Conventional Commits **type** as the PR, followed by a hyphen (no slashes):

```
fix-cursor-mcp-tool-schema
feat-restricted-policy-tool-filter
chore-bump-awx-mcp-server
```

- Use lowercase kebab-case after the type prefix
- Match the PR type (`feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, etc.)
- Do **not** use `/` in branch names (e.g. not `feat/my-change`)

```bash
git checkout -b feat-short-description   # if needed
git push -u origin HEAD
```

After pushing, check whether a PR already exists for the current branch:

```bash
gh pr view --json number,url 2>/dev/null
```

- **PR exists** → update its description (see below); do not create a new PR
- **No PR** → create one (see below)

## PR title

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format:

```
fix: strip null tool fields for Cursor MCP clients
feat: add restricted HTTP policy middleware
chore: bump awx-mcp-server to 1.2.0
```

## Create PR

```bash
gh pr create --title "feat: short description" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- ...

## Test plan
- [ ] ...

EOF
)"
gh pr edit --add-label "ai-review"
```

Return the PR URL to the user.

## Update existing PR

When pushing additional commits to a branch that already has a PR, refresh the PR description so it reflects **all** commits on the branch (not only the latest):

```bash
gh pr edit --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- ...

## Test plan
- [ ] ...

EOF
)"
```

Re-read `git log main..HEAD` and the full diff before updating. Keep the summary accurate; add or revise bullets when new changes land.

Return the PR URL to the user.

## Tests

CI runs `.github/workflows/build-and-publish.yml` on PRs and `main`/`v*` tags (multi-arch image build; push on `main` and tags). Merges to `main` also run `.github/workflows/release.yml`, which tags `vX.Y.Z` from the PR title and dispatches the image build.

Locally:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

Restricted HTTP smoke (optional; needs `.env` with `AWX_MCP_API_KEY` and AWX creds):

```bash
docker compose up --build -d
curl -sS -H "X-API-Key: $AWX_MCP_API_KEY" http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

After merge to `main`, the **Release** workflow tags `vX.Y.Z` (from the PR title) and publishes `ghcr.io/mystack-cloud/docker-awx-mcp`. Use `[skip release]` in the PR title to merge without tagging.

When the image changes behaviour deployed on core, bump `k8s_awx_mcp_image_name` in `root-infra` (`plays/paas/core/awx-test1.yml`) in a separate PR after the release image is available.

## Notes

- Repo: `mystack-cloud/docker-awx-mcp` on GitHub
- Use `gh` for all GitHub operations
- Do not push or open a PR unless the user asked
- When the user asks to push changes and a PR already exists, always update the PR description after pushing
- Canonical remote MCP setup for Cursor: `api/.cursor/rules/awx-mcp.mdc` (user-level `~/.cursor/mcp.json`)
